{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KnSVs8iJMYTFzv1uJC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nDear Dr. Pierce,\n\nI am applying for the office manager position at Brookside Family Dental. For eleven years I was the office manager at a veterinary clinic with four veterinarians and 14 staff. That practice was close in size to yours, and the work was much the same: scheduling, billing and keeping a busy front office running.\n\nIn 2014 I handled the clinic's move from paper records to AVImark practice software. I also worked on collections. Over my last three years there, unpaid invoices more than 90 days old fell from about $38,000 to $9,000.\n\nSeven years ago my mother was diagnosed with a serious illness. I gave the clinic two weeks' notice and became her full-time caregiver until she died last spring. During those years I managed her insurance claims and coordinated her appointments with six specialists. That taught me what patients need from the person who answers their questions about bills and appointments.\n\nYour posting lists Dentrix. I haven't used it yet, so I have enrolled in the 20-hour Dentrix online training course, and I will finish it before my first day. I learned AVImark from scratch when our clinic moved off paper, and I expect to learn Dentrix the same way.\n\nDr. Sue Kim, the head veterinarian at my former clinic, has agreed to be a reference.\n\nI am ready to return to full-time work, and I would welcome the chance to talk with you about the position.\n\nSincerely,\n\nLinda Marsh\n</final_document>\n\nThe letter is about 250 words. A few notes:\n\n- **What I left out:** I didn't say you trained the staff on the new software or name any results from managing people, since you weren't sure about those. The Dentrix course and Dr. Kim's reference cover those gaps better than vague claims would.\n- **What you could add:** If you'd like, put the clinic's name in the first paragraph. If you know which illness your mother had, you could swap it in for \"a serious illness,\" but the letter works without it.\n- **The email:** Since applications go by email, you could paste the letter into the email body and attach it as a PDF too. A subject line like \"Office Manager Application – Linda Marsh\" would work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":10158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1158},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f54483a-9387-4c70-82d0-a92f1dce8913","uuid":"baa07860-b81c-44f4-be7c-27a4fb50af37","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:34:28.401Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KnSMBV4apqrR5EgCcA"}
